 "summary": "Eight single Schottky barrier rectifiers in the flat SOD-123FL surface-mount package, each rated 2 A average forward current and 50 A for one 8.3 ms half-sine surge. They differ in reverse voltage, from 20 V (DSK22) to 200 V (DSK220); higher-voltage types carry a higher forward drop and lower leakage. A guard ring protects against overvoltage. Uses named for them are fast switching, circuit protection and voltage clamping. DSK210 is the 100 V type, marked K210.",
