 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "The range",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "All eight share the 2.0 A average current, 50 A surge and thermal ratings. VRRM steps from 20 V to 200 V. VF max at 2 A is 0.55 V for DSK22 and DSK24, 0.70 V for DSK25 and DSK26, 0.85 V for DSK28 and DSK210 and 0.95 V for DSK215 and DSK220. IR max at 25 °C is 0.2 mA for DSK22 to DSK26 and 0.05 mA for DSK28 to DSK220. CJ typ is 220 pF for DSK22 and DSK24 and 80 pF for DSK25 to DSK220."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature derating",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Average current holds at 2 A up to a lead temperature of about 80 °C for DSK22 to DSK26 and about 100 °C for DSK28 to DSK220, then falls in a straight line to zero at about 120 °C and 150 °C respectively."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Surge",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The 50 A peak applies to a single 8.3 ms half sine; for repeated cycles the allowed peak falls, to about 26 A at 10 cycles and about 19 A at 100."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Leakage",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Maximum reverse current at rated DC voltage is 100 times higher at 100 °C than at 25 °C for every type. On the typical curves, reverse current rises steadily with the percentage of rated peak reverse voltage applied, at both 25 °C and 100 °C junction temperature."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Mechanical",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Mould compound is rated UL 94V-0, RoHS-compliant and halogen-free. Terminals are solder plated and solderable to MIL-STD-750 method 2026. Moisture sensitivity is MSL 1 per J-STD-020, with a 260 °C lead-free reflow peak. A band on the body marks the cathode."
  }
 ],
